WEBVTT

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:11.740
The time is ripe.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:15.610
Now we will carry the Professor's plan into its final stage.

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:24.450
A total cleansing of the Earth.

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:29.350
Yes, that is the will of the Professor.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:32.260
It is the deed we must perform.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:39.460
Even after facing XX, humans continue to overrun the Earth.

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:43.400
The evil they inflict is beyond measure.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.180
Humans themselves are the very locus of the Earth's...

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:50.510
...Nay, of the universe's sickness.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:58.020
You look as though you'd like to say something.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:02:59.350
Do you have some grievance?

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:01.650
No.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:04.260
Then what is that face for?

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:07.120
You can't be saying you're opposed to the plan?

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:09.560
Don't say such nonsense.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.190
Such a thing is unthinkable, isn't it?

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:18.630
More importantly, just when did you come into a position to give orders?

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:22.980
I understand that you don't like it.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:27.920
If he so wills it, I'll immediately surrender this seat.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:41.460
Let's stop this. Our objectives are all in accord.

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:44.260
I don't care who takes command.

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.970
So long as we can carry the Professor's will into action, that is enough.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:50.700
Are you satisfied, then?

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:53.540
You can do as you like.

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:58.710
In any case, there's no more time.

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:02.710
We must bring the universe to its rightful state without delay.

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:07.920
But before that, let's welcome our comrades' return.

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:14.520
Welcome back.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:23.990
Glad to be back.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:32.400
Our preparations are complete.

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:35.710
First we will annihilate the Blattaria!

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:39.220
But those vermin have Lapis Warka.

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:42.590
No, we won't need to worry about that anymore.

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.920
We are to be granted new power.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.620
It's about time for her to return.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:00.030
Welcome back.

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:04.710
So the full complement of Gilgamesh stands in array.

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:07.270
Did you receive it from the Professor and bring it here?

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:08.740
Yes...

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:12.880
This is...

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:15.780
...that Dynamis.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.490
This is...

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:30.460
New power...

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:42.610
Let's be off to the field of battle!

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:24.720
So they've overcome the Lapis Warka?

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:36.560
They've returned from Hades, have they?

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:39.800
If so, we'll just send them back again.

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:09.360
What are you doing?

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:21.640
Why, you...

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:31.120
Perhaps we shouldn't have interfered?

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:25.130
I swear I'll squash you like a bug.

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:34.650
Their metamorphoses have a limited duration.

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:37.060
Don't back off; stand and face them!

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:39.290
Fight them all-out to the finish!

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.190
I'll decamp for the time being.

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:51.060
Go!

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:05.310
Your commander ran away and you're still going to fight anyway?

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:19.090
The Blattaria are running wild.

00:10:27.070 --> 00:10:29.840
Nobody can stop the creatures now.

00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:32.340
Now we just stand back and watch, eh?

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:57.660
Did you see them? These are their true colors.

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:06.330
They don't mind trampling others if it's for the sake of their own desires.

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:08.670
That's the kind of creatures they are.

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:12.740
That's why they need to be purified...

00:11:14.090 --> 00:11:15.990
...in the Cleansing Flood.

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:37.470
Now the contract is sealed.

00:11:38.310 --> 00:11:42.610
As of this moment, this hotel becomes the property of the House of Werdenberg.

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:47.310
I apologize for insisting on having my way to the very end.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:54.980
Allow me to say it once again: Won't you accompany us, my lady?

00:11:55.760 --> 00:12:01.130
As persons involved with the Hotel, to leave guests here while only we ourselves flee is simply...

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:05.530
I appreciate your concern, but I don't wish to get all of you mixed up in this too.

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:08.140
I truly thank you for everything up until today.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:15.500
Someday, this senseless battle will come to an end.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:20.510
At that time, I will take the liberty of buying this hotel back, my lady.

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:25.010
Yes, this place is your treasure after all.

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:50.410
You evacuate from here too.

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:52.910
No, that I cannot do, my lady.

00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:58.250
I am of a line which has served the House of Werdenberg for generations.

00:12:58.520 --> 00:13:04.690
For as long as my lady is Countess of that House, my place is here.

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:11.930
Please summon me if there is anything you need, my lady.

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:37.260
Can you still hear her?

00:13:37.430 --> 00:13:40.690
Yeah, she's calling you.

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:42.090
Huh?

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:48.400
Well?

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:52.610
No good. Like I thought, I can't hear anything.

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:58.010
Hey, if not, then how about if you put some of your Dynamis into Tatsuya, Reiko?

00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:02.310
I don't know how to do it.

00:14:02.990 --> 00:14:04.450
It's simple.

00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:06.550
Don't worry.

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:10.150
Pardon me for just a sec.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:17.800
This time try putting your forehead against Tatsuya's.

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:26.040
I wonder if this will work?

00:14:32.350 --> 00:15:02.540
Kiyoko...

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:12.980
Here it comes!

00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:15.720
Tatsuya!

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:29.200
<i>Dad is trying to destroy the world,</i>

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:32.200
<i>...this time completely,</i>

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:35.140
<i>...by means of a Cleansing Flood.</i>

00:15:37.820 --> 00:15:39.780
<i>A Cleansing Flood?</i>

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:44.580
<i>I don't really understand it, but it seems he's going to do something to the sky again.</i>

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:48.950
<i>He says by doing so, he's going to give birth to a new human race.</i>

00:15:49.890 --> 00:15:52.020
<i>He says it's because we're in the way.</i>

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:54.560
<i>He says it's because there's no value in us going on living.</i>

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:59.070
<i>But it's all right; we'll always stay together, Tatsuya.</i>

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:09.100
<i>We won't be lonely or anything.</i>

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:15.120
<i>We won't be lonely.</i>

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:20.950
Huh?

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:27.920
Kiyoko!

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:35.170
Kiyoko! Kiyoko!

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:41.300
Tatsuya! Tatsuya!

00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:53.320
What happened to me?

00:16:54.730 --> 00:16:56.320
You suddenly collapsed.

00:16:56.830 --> 00:16:58.920
Sorry, it was my fault.

00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:03.460
No, it wasn't. Tatsuya hasn't eaten anything for a long time.

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:06.970
Well then, I'll make you something.

00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:10.840
You can have a meal and then talk to your big sister again.

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:13.070
Hold on a minute.

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:17.070
Wait, I'll help too!

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:26.390
<i>Cleansing Flood?</i>

00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:41.630
After Enkidu's death, Gilgamesh, seeking eternal life, set off on a rambling journey.

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:46.110
The arduous journey spans several years,

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:50.700
...but he cannot so much as discover a means of obtaining eternal life.

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:55.350
Then one day, he reaches a certain tavern.

00:17:57.290 --> 00:18:04.160
The ale-wife, Siduri, listens to Gilgamesh's tale, and says...

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:08.500
Are you sleepy?

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:13.130
Huh? No, I'm fine. I'm not sleepy or anything.

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:18.070
Well, Siduri listens to Gilgamesh's tale and says:

00:18:18.480 --> 00:18:24.040
"Gilgamesh, whence do you direct yourself? You shall not find the life you seek."

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:25.570
"For..."

00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:29.340
"For at the creation of mankind, the gods allotted Death to men."

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:34.650
"They retained Life in their own hands."

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:39.600
"Gilgamesh, let your belly be full."

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:43.260
"Make you merry by day, and by night."

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:47.440
"Make every day a day of feasting and rejoicing."

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:49.840
"Dance and play, by day, by night."

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:52.110
"Let your clothes be sparkling and fresh."

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:54.600
"Wash your hair, and bathe your body."

00:18:55.550 --> 00:18:58.380
"Attend to the babe who holds you by the hand."

00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:02.090
"Take your wife and let her rejoice in you. For this is the lot of mankind to enjoy,"

00:19:02.090 --> 00:19:03.950
"...but immortal life is not for men."

00:19:28.880 --> 00:19:30.740
What do you suppose that was, just now?

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:45.220
I'm sorry. Somehow I felt at ease. I relaxed too much...

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:47.260
Did you wet yourself?

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:49.970
Yeah...

00:19:49.970 --> 00:19:53.370
I won't tell anyone, so hurry up and change.

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:54.830
Right...

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:20.360
There was a sound just now, wasn't there?

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:22.590
Somebody seems to be coming.

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:24.670
It may be the Blattaria.

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:34.810
Where's Toru?

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:36.340
Right now, he's just...

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:37.870
I see.

00:20:38.350 --> 00:20:41.180
At any rate, let's look into what the noise was.

00:23:25.450 --> 00:23:30.550
What we did at Heaven's Gate may have been wrong,

00:23:32.160 --> 00:23:36.650
...since as a result we sowed the seeds of many tragedies.

00:23:39.330 --> 00:23:45.770
But I'm grateful from my very heart that I can dine together with all of you here and now.

00:23:46.800 --> 00:23:50.800
I feel so happy for this stroke of fortune.

00:23:52.880 --> 00:23:54.100
Thank you.
